From: WelsonJS
Subject: [PATCH] model : support Spark-X2.5 (spark2_5)

Support the architecture "spark2_5" of the Spark-X2.5 GGUF files (for
example XHToken/Spark-X2.5-4B-GGUF, Apache-2.0), so the WelsonJS build loads
them. The fork predates the upstream support (b10828).

Backport of the C++ part of upstream llama.cpp 3ad1ba7336 ("[Model] Support
for Spark2_5ForCausalLM implementation", ggml-org/llama.cpp#27868, MIT). The
Python conversion, the chat template file and the tests are not part of it;
the GGUF files are converted upstream and carry their chat template.

1. Register the architecture: LLM_ARCH_SPARK2_5 ("spark2_5") in llama-arch,
   llama_model_mapping and the NEOX rope models (llama_model_rope_type), next
   to LLM_ARCH_STEP35. The model saver is left out: the fork lists STEP35 and
   its neighbors as unsupported there.

2. Add the pre-tokenizer "spark2_5" (LLAMA_VOCAB_PRE_TYPE_SPARK2_5, with
   clean_spaces off) with upstream's regular expressions. Its number is 58,
   after the fork's last type (FALCON_E = 57); upstream numbers it 58 after
   other types, and the number is internal.

3. Add src/models/spark2-5.cpp and its llama_model_spark2_5 in models.h:
   fused QKV projection, a sigmoid attention output gate per head, sliding
   window (512) and full attention layers from the GGUF pattern, RoPE
   dimensions and frequency bases per layer kind, RMSNorm and a GELU FFN.
   It is upstream's file with one addition: 36 layers are named 4B
   (Spark-X2.5-4B), next to upstream's 28 layers (1.7B). The fork already
   has every API it uses (create_tensor_qkv, build_qkv, wqkv_gate,
   n_rot(il), get_rope_freq_base(cparams, il), build_attn_inp_kv_iswa).

   models/*.cpp is collected by file(GLOB) in src/CMakeLists.txt, so the new
   file needs no CMake change.

---
